\x0A\x0Alcn.carrier_io_subscription_result = {\x0A  kind: \"io_subscription_result\",\x0A  conn: uint64,\x0A  sub: uint64,\x0A  ? failure: lcn.carrier_failure,\x0A}\x0A\x0Alcn.carrier_io_stop_serving = {\x0A  kind: \"io_stop_serving\",\x0A}\x0A\x0A; [SPEC RUNTIME \xC2\xA74.1, \xC2\xA76.4, \xC2\xA77.5; plan \xC2\xA72.7 steps 2-4] The Runtime\'s decision on\x0A; the dispatched Request `request` of `conn`, under the session\'s selected\x0A; `contract`:\x0A; - `failure`: refused. The host commits it, or INVALID_PARAMS when it is\x0A;   NOT_READY and the params do not validate (G171).\x0A; - otherwise admitted as `call`: the host validates the params, runs the\x0A;   provider with an invocation context whose caller is `consumer` (or\x0A;   answers `logos.schema` itself) and ends with `call_ended`, which carries\x0A;   a commitment only where `retain_request` or `retain_response` asks.\x0Alcn.carrier_admit_verdict = {\x0A  kind: \"admit_verdict\",\x0A  conn: uint64,\x0A  request: uint64,\x0A  contract: bstr .size 32,\x0A  ? failure: lcn.carrier_failure,\x0A  ? call: uint64,\x0A  ? consumer: tstr .size (1..256),\x0A  retain_request: bool,\x0A  retain_response: bool,\x0A}\x0A\x0A; [SPEC INTERFACE l.2101] Call `call` was cancelled: `is_cancelled` reads true.\x0Alcn.carrier_call_cancel = {\x0A  kind: \"call_cancel\",\x0A  call: uint64,\x0A}\x0A\x0A; The answer to a scoped step: `failure` stops the publication; `ready` (the\x0A; destination is open) answers `scoped_check`; `tag` (the delivery was\x0A; admitted; none: the subscriber\'s own decisions skipped it) answers\x0A; `scoped_admit`.\x0Alcn.carrier_scoped_result = {\x0A  kind: \"scoped_result\",\x0A  id: uint64,\x0A  ? failure: lcn.carrier_failure,\x0A  ? ready: bool,\x0A  ? tag: uint64,\x0A}\x0A"
